Signs You Need Professional Help Right Away
While some minor maintenance can be done on your own, certain warning signs mean it's time to call a professional immediately:
    • The door won't open or close at all 
    • You hear a loud bang, followed by the door refusing to move 
    • The door is visibly crooked or hanging unevenly 
    • Cables or springs are visibly frayed or snapped 
    • The opener runs but the door doesn't respond 
Attempting to fix spring or cable issues yourself can be dangerous due to the high tension involved. It's always safer — and often faster in the long run — to bring in a trained technician.

